A||N||3||cscougar||V-6 Starting Problem||||1||
Z||000000||cscougar||10-09-2000||10:45 PM||||I just this last weekend installed a low mileage 85 2.8 V-6 engine into my 85 2m4.  The engine was running when I pulled it out of a wrecked 85 2m6.  I replaced the engine, ECM, engine harness, bulkhead vacuum lines and the fuel tank with the V-6 equipment.   I put the fuses in the injector slots in the fuse panel.  <BR> <BR>Now the problem.... it wont start.   It turns over and tries to start.    I checked the schrader valve on the fuel rail and it has fuel pressure and I can hear the fuel pump come on.   I think it is electrical.  Does anyone have an idea what it could be or steps to take to find out?    As I said the engine ran the day I pulled it out....and has sat maybe about 3 months in my garage on an engine stand.  <BR> <BR>Thanks<BR> <BR>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Max The Chainsaw||10-10-2000||12:27 AM||||One thought, when you swapped out the fuel tank, did you use the 2.8 fuel pump or the one from the duke? A 2.8 has a MUCH higher fuel pressure pump than a 4 cyl does. <BR>If ya used the 2.5 pump, the 2.8 would be fuel starved and probably wouldn't start.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||10-10-2000||01:09 AM||||Did you move the distriubtor any? Plug wires correct? Fresh fuel? New fuel filter? Cold start valve ok? Good connection(s) on the MAP Sensor?||||reg||5
Z||000003||862M4inCA||10-10-2000||04:59 AM||||Have you determined if you have power to the secondary (coil side) ingition system? Also, I'd check to make sure that you have the correct firing order, and that all of the ECM connections are good and solid. Would even check the main wiring connectors into the firewall to make sure those are good and tight. ||||reg||1
